  This system forgets.
    Everything runs from memory. When the computer stops, everything you
    did here is gone: files, downloads, history, settings, installed
    programs. Nothing is written to any disk, and nothing can change that.
    Start it again and it is exactly as new. Keep nothing here you need.

  Everything goes through Tor.
    Every connection of this computer goes through the Tor network from
    the moment it starts; anything that cannot (other traffic, IPv6) is
    blocked. worm anon status shows how far Tor has connected.
    Tor Browser is in the launcher (the grid at the bottom left).

  Made for one-off tasks.
    Reading, looking something up, opening a file you do not trust,
    trying a program in a sandbox. It is not a place for real work.

  The desktop
    The Super key opens the launcher, Super+Enter a terminal, Super+Q
    closes a window, Alt+Tab switches windows, Super+I opens Settings
    (keyboard, mouse, sound, display; they last until the computer stops).
    The power icon at the bottom right has quick settings and shuts the
    computer down, and with it everything here.

  Sandboxes, inside the sandbox
    bh open lab            a disposable sandbox: no network, no files
    bh open --vm lab       the same on a kernel of its own
    bh close lab           stop it and delete what is in it

  Programs and updates
    wh install NAME        add a program, into memory (gone next time)
    worm kit install web   a set of tools at once (worm kit list)
    Update Amnesia         in the launcher: brings the USB stick up to the
                           latest version, downloading only what changed

  There is no administrator: root cannot log in, so nothing can make this
  system keep anything or reach a disk. Nothing can use a microphone or a
  camera either.
